  "body": "This fixes three editorial issues in the promise helper algorithms.\n\n### Trailing colons.\n\nFour steps that create a function with CreateBuiltinFunction end with a colon.\n\n[react](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-perform-steps-once-promise-is-settled):\n> 1. Let |onFulfilled| be CreateBuiltinFunction(|onFulfilledSteps|, 1, \"\", « »):\n> 1. Let |onRejected| be CreateBuiltinFunction(|onRejectedSteps|, 1, \"\", « »):\n\n[wait for all](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#wait-for-all):\n> 1. Let |rejectionHandler| be CreateBuiltinFunction(|rejectionHandlerSteps|, 1, \"\", « »):\n> 1. Let |fulfillmentHandler| be CreateBuiltinFunction(|fulfillmentHandler|, 1, \"\", « »):\n\nThey now end with a period, like the other CreateBuiltinFunction steps in the spec.\n\n### Reused variable name in \"wait for all\".\n\n|fulfillmentHandler| is declared twice: first for the steps, then for the function created from them.\n\n> 1. Let |fulfillmentHandler| be the following steps given |arg|:\n> 1. Let |fulfillmentHandler| be CreateBuiltinFunction(|fulfillmentHandler|, 1, \"\", « »):\n\nThe steps are renamed to |fulfillmentHandlerSteps|, matching |rejectionHandlerSteps| in the same algorithm.\n\n### Misspelling in \"wait for all\".\n\n|fullfilledCount| is renamed to |fulfilledCount|.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/webidl/1660.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 4, 2026, 7:11 AM UTC (8ac61c2)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/webidl/1660/7b9f91b...8ac61c2.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 4, 2026, 7:11 AM UTC (8ac61c2)\">Diff</a>",
